QModem Advance Modem Settings: a cell list to lock from, and tidy button rows on every tab

Neighbor Cell listed each neighbour as one run-on line ("LTE:neighbourcell:neighbourcell
intra arfcn:1725 pci:195 rsrp:-9 rsrq:-88") with a Copy button, left out the cell the modem
is actually using, and showed RSRQ as RSRP and RSRP as RSRQ: Quectel's
AT+QENG="neighbourcell" puts RSRQ in the fifth field and RSRP in the sixth, and the parser
read them the other way round. Its Lock Cell Setting and Status headers ran half the card's
width, its PCI, ARFCN and Band boxes said "undefined", there was no way to unlock, and every
lock also deleted QModem's saved re-lock-at-boot command, because the page never sent the
switch for it.

The tab is rebuilt:

- One table lists every cell the modem hears: the serving cell (and the 5G leg of an EN-DC
  link) first, marked Connected, then the neighbours by signal strength. Each row shows a
  signal meter, 4G LTE or 5G NR, the network (operator name and MCC-MNC), the band and
  frequency worked out from the ARFCN, ARFCN, PCI, RSRP, RSRQ and SINR, and the cell ID and
  TAC for the serving cell. Neighbour cells do not report their network; the row says so.
- A click on a row (or Enter) fills in the lock form; Lock on a row asks once and locks to
  that cell. For a 5G neighbour whose band could only be worked out from its ARFCN, Lock fills
  in the form and asks the user to check the band and SCS first.
- Above the table: the network, whether LTE and NR are locked and to what, Scan, and Unlock
  (shown while a lock is on). The tab scans when it opens.
- The form has real labels and help text, checks PCI (0-1007), ARFCN and band before sending,
  and has a "Keep after reboot" switch for QModem's existing boot hook
  (lockcell_boot_hook_*), reflecting its saved state.

Backend (vendor/quectel.sh, Qualcomm platform): RSRQ and RSRP are read from the right fields,
RSSI and SINR are added, each line starts with empty values so one cell's numbers never carry
over to the next, and get_neighborcell also returns "operator" (AT+COPS?) and a "serving"
array parsed from AT+QENG="servingcell" (LTE, NR5G-SA, and EN-DC's LTE + NR5G-NSA). Existing
keys keep their names and meaning, so other readers of this reply are unaffected.

The other tabs: a row of buttons at the foot of a card no longer sits on the card's edge
(Vantage pulls a card's last table into its bottom padding; createBtnRow rows get it back,
and new createActions rows sit outside the table). Rat Prefer's Submit, Reboot Modem's two
buttons and AT Debug's Clear sit in such a row; Set IMEI gets a labelled field instead of a
bare box that could read "undefined"; Reboot Modem says what soft and hard reboot do; the AT
console's buttons start at the left, 8px apart, instead of being spread across the row. No
input showed "undefined" as its placeholder or value any more.

Applies to: https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git @ 0988085b, after 0011.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

